# Milestone: M3
# Covers: chunk that registers a watcher under an explicit tag can be cancelled
#         by calling tag.stop(); cancellation causes quiescence.
#
# defer-to: T29-T31
#
# Reason: tag.stop() method-call syntax and cross-strand TAG_STOP propagation
# land at T29 (UTag + ambient-tag inheritance), T30 (OP_PUSH_TAG/OP_POP_TAG
# runtime), and T31 (urbi_tag_stop synchronous deposit + cross-strand path).
# At M3, tag scope syntax is emitted (mytag: { ... }) but UTag is not yet a
# runtime type and TAG_STOP escalates to fatal.
#
# When T31 lands, implement this fixture by uncommenting the urbiscript source
# below. Expected behaviour: the chunk registers a watcher under tag t, then
# immediately calls t.stop() to cancel it. The watcher never fires.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at T31):
#   var t = Tag.new;
#   t: every(100ms) { echo("never fires") };
#   t.stop();
#   echo("done")
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] "done"
